WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.601
In 1958, mainland China launched the Great Leap Forward.

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:08.321
People hoped production would rise quickly and catch up with advanced nations.

00:00:08.321 --> 00:00:10.825
Villagers worked day and night, full of drive.

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:14.200
Rural areas set up communal canteens, where everyone ate together.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.219
Small earthen furnaces by the fields smoked day and night.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.050
Everyone sent their household ironware to be made into steel.

00:00:21.508 --> 00:00:25.178
The radical policies brought serious problems.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:28.719
The harvest in the fields fell far short of expectations.

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:32.060
Later, food grew increasingly scarce.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.660
A severe famine broke out in many places.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.260
The food in the big pots grew less day by day.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.146
The famine caused a large number of deaths.

00:00:42.146 --> 00:00:45.019
Many villages became quiet and empty.

00:00:45.123 --> 00:00:49.437
In the cold winter, the trees had long lost their leaves.

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:53.565
This period of history left a profound lesson.

00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:56.393
People remembered that policies must match reality.
